Consider the following recursive C function that takes two arguments  <pre><code> unsigned int foo(unsigned int n, unsigned int r) {
  if (n  > 0) return (n%r +  foo (n/r, r ));
  else return 0;
}</pre></code>   <br>What is the return value of the function foo when it is called as foo (345, 10) ?

